int getDaysInMonth(String month) {
    return switch (month.toUpperCase()) {
        case "JANUARY", "MARCH", "MAY", "JULY",
             "AUGUST", "OCTOBER", "DECEMBER" -> 31;
        case "APRIL", "JUNE",
             "SEPTEMBER", "NOVEMBER"          -> 30;
        case "FEBRUARY"                        -> 28;
        default -> throw new IllegalArgumentException(
            "Invalid month: " + month
        );
    };
}

Key points: toUpperCase() normalizes input for case-insensitive matching. Comma-separated labels group months with the same day count. throw in default — switch expressions can throw exceptions as their 'value'. IllegalArgumentException for invalid input follows standard Java convention.

