sealed interface Event permits UserEvent, OrderEvent, SystemEvent {}
record UserEvent(String userId)                    implements Event {}
record OrderEvent(String orderId, double amount)   implements Event {}
record SystemEvent(String level)                   implements Event {}

void process(Event e) {
    switch (e) {
        case null                                  -> System.out.println("No event");
        case UserEvent u                           -> System.out.println("User: " + u.userId());
        case OrderEvent o when o.amount() > 5000   -> System.out.println("HIGH VALUE order: " + o.orderId());
        case OrderEvent o                          -> System.out.println("Order: " + o.orderId() + " ₹" + o.amount());
        case SystemEvent s when s.level().equals("CRITICAL") -> System.out.println("ALERT: " + s.level());
        case SystemEvent s                         -> System.out.println("System [" + s.level() + "]");
    }
}

Key: sealed interface ensures exhaustiveness (no default needed). Guarded cases (when) appear before unguarded cases of the same type. case null handles null directly. Pattern-matched variables (u, o, s) are scoped to their case arm.
